    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d606">

                <pb facs="0765" n="651" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg651"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.51/2438:Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-07-16T12:00:00-04:40"><hi rendition="#italic">July 16,
                                1924—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 11:05 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>41. Your 28, July 11, 3 p.m. Nominations of Ariza and Alvarez<anchor n="21"
                        xml:id="d606-f1"/> confirmed by the Senate yesterday and Dominican
                    Government complying with the formalities of the occasion desire to know whether
                    Ariza is <hi rendition="#italic">persona grata</hi>. Matter of short-time loan
                    of two and one half millions<anchor n="22" xml:id="d606-f2"/> was presented to
                    Congress and referred to Finance Committee of the Senate.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d606-f1" n="21" xml:id="d606-f1-content">
                <p>Frederico G. Alvarez, Secretary of the Dominican Legation.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d606-f2" n="22" xml:id="d606-f2-content">
                <p>The same loan that had previously been proposed for $2,000,000.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
